			"Message": "refactor(Element): Migrate Output build pipeline to TypeScript\n\nUpdate the Element submodule to integrate the migration of the Output build configuration from JavaScript to TypeScript. This change converts all build scripts, including the core ESBuild entry point, VS Code bundling logic, exclusion lists, and transform plugins (Inject, Replace, Rewrite, Polyfill), to strictly typed TypeScript files.\n\nThe `Source/` directory now hosts the canonical TypeScript implementations, while `Configuration/` serves as the compilation target. This ensures type safety across the build tooling and enforces PascalCase naming conventions throughout the pipeline.",
			"SHA": "ce462e68e4fdfb73324dae33f5e0125b447615c8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-09T17:33:11Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				115,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize core submodules for build refactors and logging cleanup\n\nUpdate the Element submodule to integrate upstream refactoring efforts and maintenance improvements across the Land editor stack.\n\nCocoon refactors the ESBuild configuration into a modular structure under `Configuration/ESBuild/` and introduces dedicated gRPC connection parameters for Mountain, improving pipeline maintainability. Mountain undergoes a significant refactor to strip verbose development logging (`dev_log!`, `println!`) and unused imports across over 400 files, relying instead on structured OpenTelemetry spans for observability. Rest removes dead code and unused `tokio`/`rayon` imports from its binary commands. Output and Worker submodules receive formatting passes on their respective ESBuild configurations to enhance readability.\n\nThese updates reduce binary size, clarify the signal-to-noise ratio in production logs, and align build configurations with project style guidelines.",
			"SHA": "9aaa0800ecfebc0211cb1490f47eda81742505df"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-09T16:43:33Z",
